mike (devex): Heads-up — I opened a docs PR with migration examples for the new structured output path and a short troubleshooting section for parse fallbacks: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/501

rachel (eng): Looking now. Do you rename the key or alias it at runtime? We should be explicit: server emits `tool_call` but older clients might still send `tool`.

mike (devex): We decided runtime keeps `tool_call` as canonical. Docs include a tiny shim suggestion for servers that want to accept both.

dan (ml): Add a short section showing how to validate the `arguments` string with a schema library and a fallback heuristic. Many teams fail when arguments are plain text instead of JSON.

nina (docs): Suggested text: one-sentence guardrail and a copyable schema snippet. I added an in-line example for Go and Node.

mike (devex): Can you paste the snippets here so I can quick-check formatting?

nina (docs): Sure — Node example I used:```js
const resp = await client.chat.complete(...);
const argsStr = resp.tool_call?.arguments ?? resp.tool?.args;
let args;
try {
  args = JSON.parse(argsStr);
} catch (err) {
  // fallback: treat as plain string or return a helpful error to user
  args = { _raw: String(argsStr) };
}
// validate args against a JSON Schema before invoking tool
```

nd Go example:```go
// resp is map[string]interface{} from SDK
argsRaw := ""
if tc, ok := resp["tool_call"].(map[string]interface{}); ok {
  argsRaw = tc["arguments"].(string)
} else if t, ok := resp["tool"].(map[string]interface{}); ok {
  argsRaw = t["args"].(string)
}
var args map[string]interface{}
if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(argsRaw), &args); err != nil {
  args = map[string]interface{}{"_raw": argsRaw} // fallback
}
```

rachel (eng): Nice. Two tiny asks: 1) include a one-liner sed/jq migration command for repos, 2) add a recommended unit test snippet that fakes both structured and free-form responses.

mike (devex): I'll add both. For sed I propose: `git grep -l "\"tool\"" | xargs sed -i "s/\"tool\"/\"tool_call\"/g"` — maybe show a safer perl -pi.bak variant too.

dan (ml): For the schema, include this compact one (so teams can copy-paste):```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool_call": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "arguments": {"type": "string"}
      },
      "required": ["name", "arguments"]
    }
  }
}
```

nina (docs): Also add a one-liner guardrail sentence: "Prefer `arguments` as a JSON-encoded string and validate it against a schema before using it to call external services."

ci-bot: label added: `area:structured-output`, `pr:needs-review` · preview: https://deploy.preview.redwood.ai/501

rachel (eng): tiny docs nit: don't imply SDK auto-parses arguments. Make the JS example explicit that callers must JSON.parse.

mike (devex): Will change wording to "callers should parse and validate". Also adding a short regression test suggestion: assert parser handles `{"name":"x","arguments":"{\"k\":1}"}` and the plain-text variant "please call foo with bar".

dan (ml): Suggest adding a short troubleshooting tip: if validators reject args because of single quotes or trailing commas, show a small normalization helper (replace single quotes -> double, strip trailing commas) — but call it a heuristic and warn about data loss.

nina (docs): I drafted that heuristic paragraph and flagged it as "advanced" so we don't encourage it by default.

mike (devex): Great. Once I push these edits I'll ask for a quick docs review. If CI green, I'll merge and add a changelog entry.

ci-bot: checks/presubmit: success · live-preview: queued

rachel (eng): thanks. also link to /docs/migration/shape-changes so customers can find the longer guide.

mike (devex): Done — cross-link added in PR description. Merging after preview build completes.

dan (ml): Thanks team — this should cut down support tickets about parsing.

nina (docs): Merged, closing thread. Reopen if any followups. :wave:
